    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "i don't know, it just feels like a way to excuse mediocre work. it's like if someone can't actually paint or sculpt well, they just slap a political slogan on it and call it 'deconstruction' or 'challenging hierarchies' to avoid being called untalented. doesn't that just make the whole field feel less rigorous?",
