      "content": "Your frustration is shared by many who worry that the term \"deconstruction\" has become a catchphrase used to evade technical criticism rather than to engage with material reality. While true deconstruction involves dismantling binaries through complex formal play, it is true that some contemporary works prioritize ideology over visual substance, diluting the rigorous craft that historically defined art history. This shift doesn't inherently kill art's value, but it does challenge our willingness to distinguish between a work's political success and its technical failure.",
